  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Niazicinin A may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular targets. The drug is predicted to target DNA polymerase iota, which is itself a target of Epothilone C6 and of 6,11-dihydroxy-3,3-dimethyl-10-[[(1S,2R)-5,9,10-trihydroxy-2-(2-hydroxypropan-2-yl)-6-oxo-1,2-dihydrofuro[2,3-c]xanthen-1-yl]oxy]pyrano[2,3-c]xanthen-7-one. The latter compound is also predicted to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential chain of interactions that could lead to the drug's effect on this complex. Additionally, Niazicinin A is predicted to target DNA polymerase iota, which is further targeted by 3,3'-Triiodothyronine, another compound that is predicted to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings suggest that Niazicinin A may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic pathway where Niazicinin A influences the activity of downstream targets that ultimately interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex."
